window.DOCS["6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4"]={"id":"6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4","summary":{"title_zh":"財務機制","what":"這份決議草案由第一工作組主席提出（CBD/COP/17/L.20），旨在就全球環境基金（GEF）第九次增資的認捐情形、資源配置、程序改進，以及第十次增資與第七次四年一度審查之準備等事項作出決定，以支持綱要的落實。","points":["歡迎第九次增資各參與國認捐約 44 億美元（依協議參考匯率）；並歡迎第十七次大會期間對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之認捐，約 6,000 萬美元（第 1 至 2 段）。","注意到第九次增資談判結果較第八次減少 27%，其後追加之認捐可使減幅降至約 17%，且增資期間仍對新增認捐開放；並對此減少表示關切（第 3 至 4 段）。","敦促已開發國家締約方，並邀請自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方及其他國家，依《公約》第 20 條為第九次增資出資（第 5 段）。","歡迎第九次增資的規劃方向：生物多樣性重點領域配置 35% 資源；目標為對生物多樣性的資金承諾至少 70%（依 OECD DAC 里約標記方法）；並歡迎為原住民族與地方社區設立 20% 的期望目標、對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家設立 35% 的期望基準，及對私人資本動員設立 25% 的期望目標（第 9 至 10 段）。","請全球環境基金持續改善資源配置，並加強簡化專案開發指引、降低交易成本、透過混合金融窗口促進私部門投資，以及報告撥款時程與生物多樣性相關財務的透明度（第 13 段）。","請全球環境基金深化對原住民族與地方社區的可及支持，並加強其與婦女及青年在計畫循環各階段的有效參與（第 13(g) 至 (h) 段）。","請全球環境基金於第十八次大會前，報告生物多樣性重點領域第九次增資期間的資源（以美元計）與第八次增資期間的對照數字，並分別報告小島嶼開發中國家與低度開發國家之分配（第 14 段）。","請執行秘書委託辦理第七次四年一度審查，並準備第十次增資所需資金之完整評估報告，分別提交執行附屬機構與第十八次大會（第 39 段）。","第 24 段：請執行秘書就全球生物多樣性綱要基金的盤點審查（stocktake review）進行前期準備，該審查應告知但不預設大會對第 21 條常設機構結構之決定。","第 28 段：採納附件一所列之 GEF 附加指引，涵蓋卡塔赫納議定書、名古屋議定書、生物多樣性與健康、合成生物學與性別行動計畫等領域。","第 29 至 31 段：注意到來自 45 個合格締約方的資金需求資訊，但提交數量有限，因此可供評估之資訊亦有限。"],"open":["第 12 段（要求 GEF 考量之治理與參與準則）有三種版本：全文版（含決議 17/--，以及對原住民族與地方社區、婦女與青年參與之鼓勵）、替代版一（僅引用決議 16/34 第 21 段，視情況而定）、替代版二（引用決議 16/34 與 17/--，並鼓勵上述群體參與）；尚未定案。","第 10 段之決議引用（決議 16/34 及 17/--，以及「decision(s)」之措辭）與第 13 段引用之「決議 17/--」，須待本次大會決議號碼與內容確定後定稿。","「all」一詞（第 23、25、33、38 段，以及附件三第 4(b) 段）是否限定為所有合格締約方，仍待定。","第 22(e) 段（促進所有合格締約方公平取得資金之措施）為括號文字，尚未達成共識。","第 36 段所列附件三之引用，附件三第 10 段括號內之比較研究範圍（包括以決議 16/34 其他準則為對照），以及附件三第 4(m) 段（專案永續性與耐用性指標）、第 4(n) 段（決議 16/34 所列準則）之評估標準，均為括號文字，是否納入尚未確定。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p001.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20 Distr.: Limited 30 October 2026 Original: English"},{"t":"Conference of the Parties to the"},{"t":"Convention on Biological Diversity"},{"t":"Seventeenth meeting"},{"t":"Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026"},{"t":"Agenda item 8 (b)"},{"t":"Resource mobilization and financial"},{"t":"mechanism: financial mechanism"},{"t":"Financial mechanism"},{"t":"Draft decision submitted by the Chair of Working Group I"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Recalling its decisions 15/15 of 19 December 2022 and 16/33 of 27 February 2025 pertaining to the assessment of funding needed by all eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition for the implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity 1 and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2026–June 2030),"},{"t":"Recalling also the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund contained in annex I to decision 16/33,"},{"t":"Recognizing that the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework2 is relevant to all biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements and the mandate of the Global Environment Facility,"},{"t":"1.    Welcomes the pledges made for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by participant countries, namely, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Brazil, Canada, China, Côte d’Ivoire, France, Germany, India, Ireland, Italy, Japan, Luxembourg, Mexico, Netherlands (Kingdom of the), New Zealand, Norway, Slovenia, South Africa, Spain, Switzerland, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland and Uzbekistan, which amounted to approximately 4.4 billion United States dollars, using the agreed reference exchange rates for the replenishment period;3"},{"t":"2.     Also welcomes the pledges made during the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties by Germany, Iceland, Monaco, the City of Berlin and the Province of Québec to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, which amounted to approximately 60 million dollars;"},{"t":"3.   Notes that, while the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund concluded with a reduction of 27 per cent compared with the eighth replenishment period, as indicated in the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility"},{"t":"1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"2 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"3 The initial pledges amounted to 3.9 billion dollars."}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20\n發行：限閱\n2026 年 10 月 30 日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20<br />\n發行：限閱<br />\n2026 年 10 月 30 日<br />\n原文：英文</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第十七次會議\n葉里溫，2026 年 10 月 19–30 日\n議程項目 8 (b)\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第十七次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026 年 10 月 19–30 日<br />\n議程項目 8 (b)<br />\n資源動員與財務機制：財務機制</p>","en":[3,4,5,6,7]},{"md":"財務機制\n第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案\n締約方大會，","html":"<p>財務機制<br />\n第一工作小組主席提交之決議草案<br />\n締約方大會，</p>","en":[8,9]},{"md":"**回顧**其關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，為執行《生物多樣性公約》¹及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026 年 7 月–2030 年 6 月）所需資金之決議 15/15（2022 年 12 月 19 日）及決議 16/33（2025 年 2 月 27 日），","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>其關於評估所有符合條件之開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方，為執行《生物多樣性公約》¹及其議定書，於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間（2026 年 7 月–2030 年 6 月）所需資金之決議 15/15（2022 年 12 月 19 日）及決議 16/33（2025 年 2 月 27 日），</p>","en":[10,11]},{"md":"**亦回顧**決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，","html":"<p><strong>亦回顧</strong>決議 16/33 附件一所載，關於全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資期間，公約及其議定書之四年期、以成果為導向的生物多樣性計畫優先事項框架，</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"**認識到**《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》²與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關，","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》²與所有生物多樣性相關公約及其他多邊環境協議，以及全球環境基金之職權相關，</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"1. **歡迎**參與國（即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭王國、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、西班牙、瑞士、大不列顛暨北愛爾蘭聯合王國與烏茲別克）針對全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，其金額依增資期間之議定參考匯率計算，總計約 44 億美元³；","html":"<p>1. <strong>歡迎</strong>參與國（即：澳洲、奧地利、比利時、巴西、加拿大、中國、象牙海岸、法國、德國、印度、愛爾蘭、義大利、日本、盧森堡、墨西哥、荷蘭王國、紐西蘭、挪威、斯洛維尼亞、南非、西班牙、瑞士、大不列顛暨北愛爾蘭聯合王國與烏茲別克）針對全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資所做出之承諾，其金額依增資期間之議定參考匯率計算，總計約 44 億美元³；</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"2. **亦歡迎**德國、冰島、摩納哥、柏林市及魁北克省於第十七次締約方大會期間，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金所做出之承諾，其金額約為 6,000 萬美元；","html":"<p>2. <strong>亦歡迎</strong>德國、冰島、摩納哥、柏林市及魁北克省於第十七次締約方大會期間，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金所做出之承諾，其金額約為 6,000 萬美元；</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"3. **注意到**，誠如全球環境基金理事會報告所示，全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資相比減少了 27%；","html":"<p>3. <strong>注意到</strong>，誠如全球環境基金理事會報告所示，全球環境基金信託基金第九期增資之談判結果，與第八期增資相比減少了 27%；</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"---\n¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n² 決議 15/4，附件。\n³ 初始承諾金額為 39 億美元。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n² 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n³ 初始承諾金額為 39 億美元。</p>","en":[17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p002.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties,4 the additional pledges made thereafter would indicatively bring the reduction down to 17 per cent, and the envelope remains open for new or additional pledges throughout the ninth replenishment cycle;"},{"t":"4.     Notes with concern that such a reduction comes at a time when Parties are expected to accelerate the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework;"},{"t":"5.    Urges developed country Parties, and invites other Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties and other countries, to make contributions for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund in support of the full implementation of the Framework and in accordance with the provisions of Article 20 of the Convention;"},{"t":"6.    Welcomes the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"7.    Also welcomes the improved disaggregation of co-financing by source in the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility and encourages the Facility to continue to enhance the transparency and granularity of future reporting on the various sources of co-financing;"},{"t":"8.     Notes with appreciation that the programming directions for the ninth replenishment period have been designed to deliver on all elements of the four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period adopted by the Conference of the Parties at its sixteenth meeting,5 reflecting the effective response to the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"9.     Welcomes the allocation of 35 per cent of the ninth replenishment resources to the biodiversity focal area, which is the largest focal area, and the aim of committing at least 70 per cent of funding to biodiversity over that period, according to the Rio marker methodology of the Development Assistance Committee of the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development;"},{"t":"10. Also welcomes the inclusion in the programming directions and policy recommendations of the Global Environment Facility for the ninth replenishment period of the indigenous people and local community conservation initiative, 6 an aspirational target of programming 20 per cent of resources to support indigenous peoples and local communities and strengthened support to least developed countries and small island developing States, with an aspirational benchmark of 35 per cent for those countries, as well as the introduction of the aspirational target of programming 25 per cent to mobilize private capital;"},{"t":"11. Further welcomes the establishment of the Ad Hoc Governance Working Group of the Council of the Global Environment Facility under the ninth replenishment of the Facility, in response to decision 16/33;"},{"t":"[12. Requests the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria set out in paragraph 21 of decision 16/34 and decision 17/--, ensuring a democratic and transparent system of governance that is fair, equitable, inclusive, efficient and representative, while encouraging the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth;]"},{"t":"       [12. Alt1   Requests the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria set out\nin paragraph 21 of decision 16/34, as appropriate;]\n       [12. Alt2    Requests the Global Environment Facility to take into account the criteria set out","tb":1},{"t":"in paragraph 21 of decision 16/34, and decision 17/--, while encouraging the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth;]"},{"t":"4 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1."},{"t":"5 Decision 16/33, annex I."},{"t":"6 Building on previous iterations of the Inclusive Conservation Initiative at an expanded level of 100 million dollars,"},{"t":"2/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"於提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告後所做出的額外承諾，將指示性地使減幅降至 17%，且在第九次增額週期期間，預算規模仍對新的或額外的承諾保持開放；\n4.\n**關切地注意到**，此類減幅發生在締約方預期應加速落實《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際；\n5.\n**敦促**已開發國家締約方，並**邀請**其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之國家，為全球環境基金信託基金之第九次增額做出貢獻，以支持《綱要》之全面落實，並符合《公約》第二十條之規定；\n6.\n**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；\n7.\n亦**歡迎**全球環境基金理事會報告中，按來源進行之共同融資改良後的細分，並**鼓勵**基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細緻度；\n8.\n**表示讚賞地注意到**，第九次增額期間之規劃方向，旨在落實締約方於第十六次會議上所採納之、為期四年且以成果為導向之《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性優先事項框架之所有要素，反映了對締約方所提供之指引之有效回應；\n9.\n**歡迎**將第九次增額資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標是在該期間將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；\n10. 亦**歡迎**在全球環境基金第九次增額之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，其目標為規劃 20% 的資源以支持原住民族與地方社區，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（針對該等國家之目標基準為 35%），以及引入規劃 25% 之資源以動員私人資本之願景目標；\n11. 進一步**歡迎**根據決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增額下，成立全球環境基金理事會之特設治理工作小組；\n[12. **請求**全球環境基金考量決議 16/34 第 21 段及決議 17/-- 中所列之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、包容、高效且具代表性的民主透明治理體系，同時**鼓勵**原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的全面且有效參與；]\n[12. Alt1\n**請求**全球環境基金在適當情況下，考量決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之標準；]\n[12. Alt2\n**請求**全球環境基金考量決議 16/34 第 21 段及決議 17/-- 中所列之標準，同時**鼓勵**原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的全面且有效參與；]","html":"<p>於提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告後所做出的額外承諾，將指示性地使減幅降至 17%，且在第九次增額週期期間，預算規模仍對新的或額外的承諾保持開放；<br />\n4.<br />\n<strong>關切地注意到</strong>，此類減幅發生在締約方預期應加速落實《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之際；<br />\n5.<br />\n<strong>敦促</strong>已開發國家締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之國家，為全球環境基金信託基金之第九次增額做出貢獻，以支持《綱要》之全面落實，並符合《公約》第二十條之規定；<br />\n6.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會提交予第十七次締約方大會之報告；<br />\n7.<br />\n亦<strong>歡迎</strong>全球環境基金理事會報告中，按來源進行之共同融資改良後的細分，並<strong>鼓勵</strong>基金持續提升未來關於各類共同融資來源報告之透明度與細緻度；<br />\n8.<br />\n<strong>表示讚賞地注意到</strong>，第九次增額期間之規劃方向，旨在落實締約方於第十六次會議上所採納之、為期四年且以成果為導向之《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性優先事項框架之所有要素，反映了對締約方所提供之指引之有效回應；<br />\n9.<br />\n<strong>歡迎</strong>將第九次增額資源之 35% 分配至生物多樣性重點領域（此為最大之重點領域），且根據經濟合作暨發展組織開發援助委員會之里約標記法（Rio marker methodology），其目標是在該期間將至少 70% 的資金投入於生物多樣性；<br />\n10. 亦<strong>歡迎</strong>在全球環境基金第九次增額之規劃方向與政策建議中，納入原住民族與地方社區保育倡議，其目標為規劃 20% 的資源以支持原住民族與地方社區，並加強對低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家的支持（針對該等國家之目標基準為 35%），以及引入規劃 25% 之資源以動員私人資本之願景目標；<br />\n11. 進一步<strong>歡迎</strong>根據決議 16/33，在全球環境基金第九次增額下，成立全球環境基金理事會之特設治理工作小組；<br />\n[12. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金考量決議 16/34 第 21 段及決議 17/-- 中所列之標準，確保建立一個公平、公正、包容、高效且具代表性的民主透明治理體系，同時<strong>鼓勵</strong>原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的全面且有效參與；]<br />\n[12. Alt1<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金在適當情況下，考量決議 16/34 第 21 段所列之標準；]<br />\n[12. Alt2<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金考量決議 16/34 第 21 段及決議 17/-- 中所列之標準，同時<strong>鼓勵</strong>原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的全面且有效參與；]</p>","en":[6,7,8,9,10]},{"md":"4 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n5 決議 16/33，附件 I。\n6 在擴大至 1 億美元規模之基礎上，延續先前版本之包容性保育倡議，","html":"<p>4 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.<br />\n5 決議 16/33，附件 I。<br />\n6 在擴大至 1 億美元規模之基礎上，延續先前版本之包容性保育倡議，</p>","en":[11,12,13,14,15]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p003.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"13. Also requests the Global Environment Facility to accelerate efforts to further strengthen its effectiveness, including by:"},{"t":"(a) Improving integration pathways, approaches and integrated programmes that deliver system-wide environmental benefits to improve synergies among environmental conventions, while ensuring that such programmes take into account their respective mandates, remain country-driven, responsive to national circumstances and priorities, and implemented through meaningful engagement with national executing agencies from recipient countries;"},{"t":"(b) Enabling and facilitating private sector financing aligned with the objectives of the Convention through its blended finance programme funding window and the provision of predictable support to eligible Parties, with a view to developing projects and programmes that enable greater private sector investment and financial flows, including through long-term enabling policy frameworks, incentives, regulations, blended finance tools and the development of financially viable, investment-ready biodiversity finance projects and pipelines, while recognizing that such investments complement public finance;"},{"t":"(c) Promoting whole-of-society and whole-of-government approaches, as appropriate and in accordance with national circumstances, to strengthen programme and project ownership at the national level and the alignment of biodiversity actions with nationally identified priorities, national biodiversity strategies and action plans, national development priorities, and policy coherence;"},{"t":"(d) Continuing to improve its resource allocation, including by continuing to maximize the generation of global environmental benefits and recognizing the contribution of indigenous peoples and local communities in achieving them, and to take into account the needs and national priorities of developing countries;"},{"t":"(e) Continuing to improve the performance of its implementing agencies by enhancing transparency, equity, predictability and responsiveness to the specific needs and priorities of developing country Parties in the context of paragraphs 5, 6 and 7 of Article 20 of the Convention, as identified by countries in their projects;"},{"t":"(f)    Sustaining enhanced support for all eligible Parties, in particular in the context of paragraphs 5, 6 and 7 of Article 20 of the Convention, by reducing transaction costs, simplifying access across existing Global Environment Facility focal areas and financing windows, including through the appropriate national, regional and multilateral implementing agencies, and improving the timeliness and predictability of financial support, measured by the date of first disbursement to the recipient country;"},{"t":"(g) Deepening accessible support for indigenous peoples and local communities, in line with element 8 of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 20307 (access, including direct access, to funding for indigenous peoples and local communities for the conservation, restoration and sustainable use of biodiversity), including by developing guidance on the 20 per cent portfolio-wide target for indigenous peoples and local communities, taking into consideration the need for their effective participation along the project cycle, including through simplified access modalities, in line with national legislation and circumstances, with transparent accounting of intermediary costs;"},{"t":"(h) Strengthening the effective participation of indigenous people and local communities, women and youth at all stages of the project cycle, including in project decision-making, in accordance with the national legislation of the Parties concerned;"},{"t":"(i)   Continuing to promote country-driven national initiatives and regionally coordinated regional and multi-country initiatives, including transboundary initiatives, with the effective"},{"t":"7 Decision 16/4, annex."},{"t":"3/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"13. 亦**請求**全球環境基金加速其努力以進一步強化其成效，包括透過：\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統性的環境效益，並增進環境公約之間的綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自的職權，保持由國家驅動，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構的實質參與來執行；\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，以及向符合條件之締約方提供可預測的支援，使符合《公約》目標之私部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目標在於開發能促進更大規模私部門投資與資金流動之專案與計畫，包括透過長期之賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具投資準備度之生物多樣性金融專案與案源，同時承認此類投資與公共財政相輔相成；\n(c) 在適當且符合國家情況下，推動全社會與全政府方法，以強化國家層級之計畫與專案自主權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家所識別之優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性相結合；\n(d) 持續改進其資源配置，包括持續極大化全球環境效益之產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在達成效益中所做的貢獻，且考量開發中國家之需求與國家優先事項；\n(e) 藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，以及對開發中國家締約方在《公約》第20條第5、6及7項背景下（依各國於其專案中所識別之需求）特定需求與優先事項之回應能力，持續改進其執行機構之績效；\n(f) 透過降低交易成本、簡化跨越現有全球環境基金焦點領域與資助窗口之取得途徑（包括透過適當的國家、區域與多邊執行機構），並改善財務支援的及時性與可預測性（以對受援國之首次撥款日期衡量），以維持對所有符合條件之締約方之強化支援，特別是在《公約》第20條第5、6及7項之背景下；\n(g) 根據第八條(j)工作計畫之第8要素，以及《公約》中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他關於2030年之規定（包括原住民族與地方社區在生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用方面取得資金之途徑，包括直接取得資金），深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得性支援，包括針對原住民族與地方社區之20%全組合目標開發指引，並考量其在專案週期中有效參與之需求，包括透過符合國家立法與情況之簡化取得模式，並對中間成本進行透明的核算；\n7 決議 16/4，附件。","html":"<p>13. 亦<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金加速其努力以進一步強化其成效，包括透過：<br />\n(a) 改進整合路徑、方法與整合計畫，以提供全系統性的環境效益，並增進環境公約之間的綜效，同時確保此類計畫考量其各自的職權，保持由國家驅動，並回應國家情況與優先事項，且透過與受援國國家執行機構的實質參與來執行；<br />\n(b) 透過其混合金融計畫之資助窗口，以及向符合條件之締約方提供可預測的支援，使符合《公約》目標之私部門融資得以實現並獲得促進，其目標在於開發能促進更大規模私部門投資與資金流動之專案與計畫，包括透過長期之賦能政策框架、激勵措施、法規、混合金融工具，以及開發具財務可行性且具投資準備度之生物多樣性金融專案與案源，同時承認此類投資與公共財政相輔相成；<br />\n(c) 在適當且符合國家情況下，推動全社會與全政府方法，以強化國家層級之計畫與專案自主權，並使生物多樣性行動與國家所識別之優先事項、國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫、國家發展優先事項以及政策一致性相結合；<br />\n(d) 持續改進其資源配置，包括持續極大化全球環境效益之產生，並承認原住民族與地方社區在達成效益中所做的貢獻，且考量開發中國家之需求與國家優先事項；<br />\n(e) 藉由增進透明度、公平性、可預測性，以及對開發中國家締約方在《公約》第20條第5、6及7項背景下（依各國於其專案中所識別之需求）特定需求與優先事項之回應能力，持續改進其執行機構之績效；<br />\n(f) 透過降低交易成本、簡化跨越現有全球環境基金焦點領域與資助窗口之取得途徑（包括透過適當的國家、區域與多邊執行機構），並改善財務支援的及時性與可預測性（以對受援國之首次撥款日期衡量），以維持對所有符合條件之締約方之強化支援，特別是在《公約》第20條第5、6及7項之背景下；<br />\n(g) 根據第八條(j)工作計畫之第8要素，以及《公約》中與原住民族與地方社區相關之其他關於2030年之規定（包括原住民族與地方社區在生物多樣性保育、復育與永續利用方面取得資金之途徑，包括直接取得資金），深化對原住民族與地方社區之可取得性支援，包括針對原住民族與地方社區之20%全組合目標開發指引，並考量其在專案週期中有效參與之需求，包括透過符合國家立法與情況之簡化取得模式，並對中間成本進行透明的核算；<br />\n7 決議 16/4，附件。</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"(h) 根據相關締約方之國家立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年在專案週期各階段（包括在專案決策中）之有效參與；\n(i) 持續推動由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域性且跨國性之區域與多國倡議（包括跨境倡議），並有效促成","html":"<p>(h) 根據相關締約方之國家立法，強化原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年在專案週期各階段（包括在專案決策中）之有效參與；<br />\n(i) 持續推動由國家驅動之國家倡議，以及區域性且跨國性之區域與多國倡議（包括跨境倡議），並有效促成</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p004.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"participation of national focal points for the Convention and relevant national authorities and formal approval of operational focal points for the Global Environment Facility;"},{"t":"(j)    Ensuring that Global Environment Facility support for the implementation of the Convention, in particular the national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national targets, is country-led;"},{"t":"(k) Continuing to support the development and implementation of national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments and their integration, where applicable, into national policies and priorities;"},{"t":"(l)    Continuing to advance collaboration, coherence and complementarity across multilateral climate funds and other sources of finance relevant to the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"(m) Strengthening national institutional and technical capacities for project preparation, implementation, monitoring and reporting;"},{"t":"(n)    Simplifying project development guidance;"},{"t":"(o) Reporting on the attainment of the targets mentioned in paragraph 9 above and on disaggregated data on programming, approvals and disbursement by recipient country or region;"},{"t":"(p) Improving the transparency and granularity of reporting on biodiversity-related finance, including by distinguishing between financing for which biodiversity is a principal objective and financing for which it is a significant objective under the Rio marker methodology, taking into account the qualitative nature of the Rio markers and by clarifying the extent to which such financing contribute to the implementation of the Framework;"},{"t":"14. Further requests the Global Environment Facility to report to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting on the resources of the biodiversity focal area for the ninth replenishment period of its Trust Fund expressed in United States dollars at the final replenishment level, together with the corresponding figure for the eighth replenishment period, and on the share of resources originally programmed and subsequently disbursed to small island developing States, presented separately from least developed countries;"},{"t":"15. Recognizes the value of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund in complementing the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund by providing financial support to eligible developing country Parties for achieving the goals and targets of the Framework;"},{"t":"16. Welcomes the progress made by the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund with a one-step approval process and the achievement to date of the three portfolio targets set forth in the programming directions for the Fund;8"},{"t":"17. Takes note of the information on the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund contained in the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"18. Recalls paragraph 14 of decision 16/33, emphasizing the need to further scale up new and additional resources from all sources to match the ambition of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, in accordance with paragraphs 19 and 20 of decision 15/15, while recognizing that many eligible Parties have not yet received support from the Fund;"},{"t":"19. Reiterates the call made by the Council of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund at its sixth meeting for new and additional contributions from all sources to support the continuous, rapid and robust capitalization of the Fund, in line with Target 19 of the Kunming-Montreal Global"},{"t":"8 Global Environment Facility, document GEF/C.64/06/Rev/02."},{"t":"4/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"公約國家聯絡點及相關國家主管機關之參與，以及全球環境基金執行聯絡點之正式核准；\n(j)\n確保全球環境基金對履行公約（特別是國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標）之支持，係由國家主導；\n(k)\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具之制定與實施，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；\n(l)\n持續推進多邊氣候基金與其他與履行綱要相關之資金來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；\n(m)\n強化國家在專案準備、實施、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；\n(n)","html":"<p>公約國家聯絡點及相關國家主管機關之參與，以及全球環境基金執行聯絡點之正式核准；<br />\n(j)<br />\n確保全球環境基金對履行公約（特別是國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標）之支持，係由國家主導；<br />\n(k)<br />\n持續支持國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具之制定與實施，並在適用情況下將其納入國家政策與優先事項；<br />\n(l)<br />\n持續推進多邊氣候基金與其他與履行綱要相關之資金來源之間的協作、一致性與互補性；<br />\n(m)<br />\n強化國家在專案準備、實施、監測與報告方面的制度與技術能力；<br />\n(n)</p>","en":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"md":"簡化專案開發指南；","html":"<p>簡化專案開發指南；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(o)\n報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之規劃、核准與撥款之分項資料；\n(p)\n提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標之融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標之融資，並考量里約標記的性質，且釐清此類融資對履行綱要之貢獻程度；\n14. **進一步請求**全球環境基金在其第十八次締約方大會上，報告其信託基金第九期增資期間，以最終增補水平表示之生物多樣性重點領域資源（以美元表示），並附上第八期增資期間之對應資料，以及原先規劃並隨後撥付予小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例，且須與低度開發國家分開呈現；\n15. **認識到**全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要之目標與指標；\n16. **歡迎**全球生物多樣性綱要基金透過單一步驟核准程序所取得的進展，以及迄今為止達成基金規劃方向中所設定之三個投資組合目標之成就；$^8$\n17. **注意到**全球環境基金理事會於第十七次締約方大會報告中所包含之關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊；\n18. **回顧**決議 16/33 第 14 段，強調根據決議 15/15 第 19 及 20 段，需進一步擴大來自所有來源之新且額外資源，以匹配昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之雄心，同時認可許多符合條件之締約方尚未獲得基金之支持；\n19. **重申**全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會於其第六次會議上之呼籲，即要求來自所有來源之新且額外貢獻，以支持基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，並與昆明－蒙特婁全球","html":"<p>(o)<br />\n報告上述第 9 段所述目標之達成情況，以及按受援國家或區域分類之規劃、核准與撥款之分項資料；<br />\n(p)<br />\n提高生物多樣性相關財務報告的透明度與細粒度，包括根據里約標記（Rio marker）方法論，區分以生物多樣性為主要目標之融資與以生物多樣性為重要目標之融資，並考量里約標記的性質，且釐清此類融資對履行綱要之貢獻程度；<br />\n14. <strong>進一步請求</strong>全球環境基金在其第十八次締約方大會上，報告其信託基金第九期增資期間，以最終增補水平表示之生物多樣性重點領域資源（以美元表示），並附上第八期增資期間之對應資料，以及原先規劃並隨後撥付予小島嶼開發中國家的資源比例，且須與低度開發國家分開呈現；<br />\n15. <strong>認識到</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金在補充全球環境基金信託基金方面的價值，透過為符合條件的開發中國家締約方提供財務支持，以實現綱要之目標與指標；<br />\n16. <strong>歡迎</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金透過單一步驟核准程序所取得的進展，以及迄今為止達成基金規劃方向中所設定之三個投資組合目標之成就；<sup>8</sup><br />\n17. <strong>注意到</strong>全球環境基金理事會於第十七次締約方大會報告中所包含之關於全球生物多樣性綱要基金的資訊；<br />\n18. <strong>回顧</strong>決議 16/33 第 14 段，強調根據決議 15/15 第 19 及 20 段，需進一步擴大來自所有來源之新且額外資源，以匹配昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之雄心，同時認可許多符合條件之締約方尚未獲得基金之支持；<br />\n19. <strong>重申</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金理事會於其第六次會議上之呼籲，即要求來自所有來源之新且額外貢獻，以支持基金持續、快速且穩健的資本化，並與昆明－蒙特婁全球</p>","en":[7,8,9,10,11]},{"md":"---\n$^8$ 全球環境基金，文件 GEF/C.64/06/Rev/02。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>8</sup> 全球環境基金，文件 GEF/C.64/06/Rev/02。</p>","en":[12,13,14,15]},{"md":"4/15","html":"<p>4/15</p>","en":[16]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p005.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"Biodiversity Framework and without affecting existing obligations under Article 20 of the Convention;"},{"t":"20. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund to enhance efforts to mobilize predictable, adequate and additional resources from all sources and report on the implementation of its resource mobilization strategy for the period from July 2026 to June 2030, including through disaggregated information on pledges and contributions paid by sources of finance;"},{"t":"21. Invites developed country Parties and Parties that voluntarily assume the obligations of developed country Parties, other governments at all levels, the private sector and philanthropic organizations to make or increase their contributions to the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;"},{"t":"22. Requests the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund and its implementing agencies to continue to enhance its efforts to:"},{"t":"(a) Facilitate, as appropriate, the mobilization of financial resources from all sources, recognizing the need for further capitalization;"},{"t":"(b) Improve co-financing arrangements, as appropriate, while recognizing that co-financing is not a requirement, without creating additional barriers to access or shifting the financial burden to all eligible countries, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and taking into consideration the specific needs of vulnerable countries, in the context of paragraphs 6 and 7 of Article 20 of the Convention;"},{"t":"(c) Reduce, where appropriate and taking into account country ownership, project cycle processing times, including for the disbursement and endorsement processes of approved projects, through transparent, predictable and time-bound procedures, and streamline implementation;"},{"t":"(d) Report on average processing and disbursement times disaggregated for least developed countries and small island developing States, and other eligible Parties by region;"},{"t":"[(e) Enhance equitable access, including by considering measures to facilitate access for all eligible country Parties, including those that are yet to receive support from the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund;]"},{"t":"23. Requests the Global Environment Facility, in collaboration with the Executive Secretary, to provide, within their respective mandates, support to [all] eligible Parties, upon request, for:"},{"t":"(a) Project preparation, capacity-building and the tracking of ongoing biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities, as necessary, including, where applicable, through national coordination mechanisms, such as country platforms or national steering committees;"},{"t":"(b) The preparation and submission of national reports on the implementation of the Convention, the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety9 and the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, taking into account national circumstances;10"},{"t":"(c) Capacity-building for leveraging private sector financing, including from capital markets, through, inter alia, innovative mechanisms and blended finance, and for developing financially viable projects, with robust environmental, social and financial safeguards, taking into account debt vulnerabilities;"},{"t":"24. Requests the Executive Secretary to undertake preparatory work for the stocktake review of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund referred to in paragraph 29 of decision 15/15, in accordance with annex III to the present decision, in conjunction with its seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, recognizing that the stocktake shall inform, but not"},{"t":"9 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"10 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619."},{"t":"5/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"生物多樣性綱要，且不影響《公約》第 20 條下既有義務之履行；","html":"<p>生物多樣性綱要，且不影響《公約》第 20 條下既有義務之履行；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"20. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外資源之努力，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略之執行情況，包括透過按財務來源分類之承諾與已支付貢獻金之細分資訊；","html":"<p>20. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金加強從所有來源動員可預測、充足且額外資源之努力，並報告其 2026 年 7 月至 2030 年 6 月期間資源動員策略之執行情況，包括透過按財務來源分類之承諾與已支付貢獻金之細分資訊；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"21. **邀請**已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；","html":"<p>21. <strong>邀請</strong>已開發國家締約方、自願承擔已開發國家締約方義務之締約方、各級其他政府、私營部門及慈善組織，對全球生物多樣性綱要基金進行或增加其貢獻；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"22. **請求**全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：","html":"<p>22. <strong>請求</strong>全球生物多樣性綱要基金及其執行機構繼續加強其努力以：</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(a) 在適當情況下，促進從所有來源動員財務資源，並承認進一步增資之必要性；","html":"<p>(a) 在適當情況下，促進從所有來源動員財務資源，並承認進一步增資之必要性；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(b) 在《公約》第 20 條第 6 段及第 7 段之背景下，在適當情況下改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成取得資源之額外障礙，亦不應將財務負擔轉嫁至所有符合資格之國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並考量脆弱國家之特定需求；","html":"<p>(b) 在《公約》第 20 條第 6 段及第 7 段之背景下，在適當情況下改善共同融資安排，同時承認共同融資並非必要條件，且不應造成取得資源之額外障礙，亦不應將財務負擔轉嫁至所有符合資格之國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，並考量脆弱國家之特定需求；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(c) 在適當情況下，並考量國家自主權，透過透明、可預測且有時限之程序，縮短專案週期處理時間，包括已核准專案之撥款與核准程序，並簡化執行流程；","html":"<p>(c) 在適當情況下，並考量國家自主權，透過透明、可預測且有時限之程序，縮短專案週期處理時間，包括已核准專案之撥款與核准程序，並簡化執行流程；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(d) 按區域針對低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及其他符合資格之締約方，報告平均處理與撥款時間之細分資料；","html":"<p>(d) 按區域針對低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家及其他符合資格之締約方，報告平均處理與撥款時間之細分資料；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"[(e) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施以促進所有符合資格之締約方取得資源，包括那些尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之締約方；]","html":"<p>[(e) 加強公平取得，包括考慮採取措施以促進所有符合資格之締約方取得資源，包括那些尚未獲得全球生物多樣性綱要基金支持之締約方；]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"23. **請求**全球環境基金與執行秘書合作，在其各自職權範圍內，應依請求為[所有]符合資格之締約方提供以下支持：","html":"<p>23. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金與執行秘書合作，在其各自職權範圍內，應依請求為[所有]符合資格之締約方提供以下支持：</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"(a) 視必要情況，進行專案準備、能力建構以及追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項，包括在適用情況下，透過國家協調機制（例如國家平台或國家指導委員會）進行；","html":"<p>(a) 視必要情況，進行專案準備、能力建構以及追蹤進行中之生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項，包括在適用情況下，透過國家協調機制（例如國家平台或國家指導委員會）進行；</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"(b) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於履行《公約》、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書⁹以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其所產生利益名古屋議定書》之國家報告；¹⁰","html":"<p>(b) 考量國家情況，編製並提交關於履行《公約》、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書⁹以及《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其所產生利益名古屋議定書》之國家報告；¹⁰</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"(c) 透過（除其他方式外）創新機制與混合融資，加強利用來自（包括來自資本市場）私營部門融資之能力建構，以及開發具備穩健環境、社會與財務保障且具財務可行性之專案，並考量債務脆弱性；","html":"<p>(c) 透過（除其他方式外）創新機制與混合融資，加強利用來自（包括來自資本市場）私營部門融資之能力建構，以及開發具備穩健環境、社會與財務保障且具財務可行性之專案，並考量債務脆弱性；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"24. **請求**執行秘書根據本決議附件 III，配合財務機制有效性之第七次四年一度審查，為決議 15/15 第 29 段所提之全球生物多樣性綱要基金盤點審查進行準備工作，並承認該盤點應提供資訊，但不","html":"<p>24. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書根據本決議附件 III，配合財務機制有效性之第七次四年一度審查，為決議 15/15 第 29 段所提之全球生物多樣性綱要基金盤點審查進行準備工作，並承認該盤點應提供資訊，但不</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"---\n⁹ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n¹⁰ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁹ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n¹⁰ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[15,16]},{"md":"5/15","html":"<p>5/15</p>","pre":" 3008 卷，第 30619 號。\n\n","en":[17]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p006.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"prejudge, consideration by the Conference of the Parties of the permanent institutional structure of the financial mechanism provided under Article 21 of the Convention;"},{"t":"25. Requests the Global Environment Facility to facilitate the provision of financial support for [all] eligible Parties in a timely manner for the development of national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national targets and the preparation of eighth national reports by the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"26. Also requests the Global Environment Facility, in consultation with recipient countries and the Executive Secretary, to review the effectiveness of projects funded during its seventh and eighth cycles for the development of national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national reports under the Convention and its Protocols and to report on the measures that it has taken to address identified challenges for the preparation of the eighth national report to the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"27. Requests the Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Secretariat of the Global Environment Facility, to prepare a draft four-year outcome-oriented framework of biodiversity programme priorities of the Convention and its Protocols related to the use of Facility resources for biodiversity for the period from July 2030 to June 2034, taking into consideration the global review of collective progress in the implementation of the Framework, as well as access modalities and capacity constraints of developing countries Parties, in particular least developed countries and small island developing States, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and subsequent adoption by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"28. Adopts the additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility contained in annex I to the present decision, and requests the Council of the Global Environment Facility to include information regarding the implementation of the additional guidance in its reports to the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"29. Notes the information on funding needs received from 45 eligible Parties and the compilation and analysis of that information transmitted by the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity to the Global Environment Facility to help with the negotiations for the ninth replenishment of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;"},{"t":"30. Takes note of the report on the assessment of the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;11"},{"t":"31. Notes the limited number of submissions from eligible Parties and therefore limited information available for assessing the amount of funds needed for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework for the ninth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund;"},{"t":"32. Also notes the importance of a realistic assessment of funding necessary and available for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols and the Framework for future replenishment periods of the Global Environment Facility;"},{"t":"33. Emphasizes the need to continue to strengthen technical and institutional support for [all] eligible Parties, so that their needs are fully reflected in future assessments;"},{"t":"34. Adopts the terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention to inform, if appropriate, the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund"},{"t":"11 CBD/COP/17/INF/13."},{"t":"6/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"預判、締約方大會對《公約》第21條規定之財務機制永久性制度結構之審議；","html":"<p>預判、締約方大會對《公約》第21條規定之財務機制永久性制度結構之審議；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"25. **請求**全球環境基金促進及時為[所有]合資格締約方提供財務支持，以進行國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標之制定，並在第十八次締約方大會召開前完成第八次國家報告之編製；","html":"<p>25. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金促進及時為[所有]合資格締約方提供財務支持，以進行國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家目標之制定，並在第十八次締約方大會召開前完成第八次國家報告之編製；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"26. **亦請求**全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為履行《公約》及其議定書下之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助之專案成效，並在第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議上，向執行附屬機構報告其為應對第八次國家報告編製過程中所發現之挑戰所採取之措施；","html":"<p>26. <strong>亦請求</strong>全球環境基金在諮詢受援國與執行秘書後，審查其第七與第八週期期間，為履行《公約》及其議定書下之國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家報告所資助之專案成效，並在第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議上，向執行附屬機構報告其為應對第八次國家報告編製過程中所發現之挑戰所採取之措施；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"27. **請求**執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量對《綱要》實施集體進展之全球審查，以及開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，準備一份以成果為導向之、關於《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期草案框架，該框架涉及2030年7月至2034年6月期間利用基金資源於生物多樣性之用途，以供執行附屬機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議審議，並隨後由締約方大會於其第十八次會議予以通過；","html":"<p>27. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在諮詢全球環境基金秘書處後，考量對《綱要》實施集體進展之全球審查，以及開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之取得模式與能力限制，準備一份以成果為導向之、關於《公約》及其議定書生物多樣性計畫優先事項之四年期草案框架，該框架涉及2030年7月至2034年6月期間利用基金資源於生物多樣性之用途，以供執行附屬機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前之一次會議審議，並隨後由締約方大會於其第十八次會議予以通過；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"28. **通過**本決議附件一所載之全球環境基金附加指南，並**請求**全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關實施該附加指南之資訊；","html":"<p>28. <strong>通過</strong>本決議附件一所載之全球環境基金附加指南，並<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金理事會在提交予締約方大會之報告中，納入有關實施該附加指南之資訊；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"29. **注意到**從45個合資格締約方收到之資金需求資訊，以及生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資談判之該等資訊之彙編與分析；","html":"<p>29. <strong>注意到</strong>從45個合資格締約方收到之資金需求資訊，以及生物多樣性公約秘書處傳送予全球環境基金以協助全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資談判之該等資訊之彙編與分析；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"30. **注意到**關於全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額之評估報告；$^{11}$","html":"<p>30. <strong>注意到</strong>關於全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書所需資金金額之評估報告；<sup>11</sup></p>","en":[7]},{"md":"31. **注意到**來自合資格締約方之提交件數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》所需資金金額之可用資訊有限；","html":"<p>31. <strong>注意到</strong>來自合資格締約方之提交件數量有限，因此對於評估全球環境基金信託基金第九次增資期間，為實施《公約》及其議定書與《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》所需資金金額之可用資訊有限；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"32. **亦注意到**對於全球環境基金未來增資週期，進行實施《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用資金之務實評估具有重要性；","html":"<p>32. <strong>亦注意到</strong>對於全球環境基金未來增資週期，進行實施《公約》及其議定書與《綱要》所需且可用資金之務實評估具有重要性；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"33. **強調**有必要繼續加強對[所有]合資格締約方之技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映於未來之評估中；","html":"<p>33. <strong>強調</strong>有必要繼續加強對[所有]合資格締約方之技術與制度支持，以使其需求能充分反映於未來之評估中；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"34. **通過**關於全面評估所需資金金額之任務說明書，該資金旨在根據締約方提供之指南，協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下之承諾，以在適當時提供資訊予全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期間。","html":"<p>34. <strong>通過</strong>關於全面評估所需資金金額之任務說明書，該資金旨在根據締約方提供之指南，協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及轉型經濟體締約方履行其在《公約》下之承諾，以在適當時提供資訊予全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期間。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"---\n$^{11}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/13.","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>11</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/13.</p>","en":[12,13]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p007.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"(July 2030–June 2034), as contained in annex II to the present decision, noting that the assessment should be conducted in a manner that avoids disproportionate administrative burdens and provides for financial and technical support for data collection in developing country Parties;"},{"t":"35. Invites Parties to establish coordination mechanisms for planning and monitoring biodiversity projects that are accessible to stakeholders and regularly updated, as appropriate;"},{"t":"36. Adopts the terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism[, as contained in annex III to the present decision];"},{"t":"37. Invites Parties, other Governments and relevant organizations, as well as indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, to contribute to and participate in the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as outlined in the terms of reference;"},{"t":"38. Emphasizes the importance of integrating in the quadrennial review specific indicators for [all] eligible Parties, in particular on the number of projects funded, disbursement times and impact on local communities;"},{"t":"39.     Requests the Executive Secretary:"},{"t":"(a) To commission and make available a report on the seventh quadrennial review of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism in time for consideration by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"(b) To prepare a report on the full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and by the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting;"},{"t":"(c) Subject to the availability of resources, to further strengthen collaboration and engagement with relevant financial institutions and stakeholders, in order to accelerate the implementation of the Framework, with an emphasis on improving access modalities;"},{"t":"(d) To report, as applicable, on the results of the collaboration and engagement mentioned in the subparagraph above, and include options for such engagements, to the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(e) To facilitate, as applicable, the effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth in the implementation of the activities referred to in subparagraphs (a) to (d) above."},{"t":"Annex I*"},{"t":"Additional guidance to the Global Environment Facility"},{"t":"Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety"},{"t":"1.      The Global Environment Facility is requested:"},{"t":"(a) To make dedicated adequate and timely funding available to eligible Parties, in particular the least developed countries and the small island developing States, for putting in place legal, administrative and other measures for implementing the Cartagena Protocol, including the long-term strengthening of national implementation capacities;"},{"t":"* The present annex is being issued without formal editing."},{"t":"7/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月），如本決議附件 II 所載，注意到評估應以避免不成比例的行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中國家締約方的資料收集提供財務與技術支援；","html":"<p>（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月），如本決議附件 II 所載，注意到評估應以避免不成比例的行政負擔之方式進行，並為開發中國家締約方的資料收集提供財務與技術支援；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"35. **邀請**締約方建立生物多樣性計畫之規劃與監測協調機制，並視情況確保利害關係人可取得該機制，且定期更新；","html":"<p>35. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方建立生物多樣性計畫之規劃與監測協調機制，並視情況確保利害關係人可取得該機制，且定期更新；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"36. **採納**財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍[, 如本決議附件 III 所載]；","html":"<p>36. <strong>採納</strong>財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍[, 如本決議附件 III 所載]；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"37. **邀請**締約方、其他政府及相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為職權範圍所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；","html":"<p>37. <strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及相關組織，以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年，參與並為職權範圍所概述之財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查做出貢獻；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"38. **強調**在四年一度審查中，針對 [所有] 符合資格之締約方納入特定指標之重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；","html":"<p>38. <strong>強調</strong>在四年一度審查中，針對 [所有] 符合資格之締約方納入特定指標之重要性，特別是關於資助計畫數量、撥款時間以及對地方社區之影響；</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"39. **請求**執行秘書：","html":"<p>39. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書：</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；","html":"<p>(a) 委託並及時提供一份關於財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之報告，以供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(b) 根據締約方所提供之指引，準備一份關於為協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方）履行《公約》義務所需資金總額之全面評估報告，以供執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；該評估係針對全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期；","html":"<p>(b) 根據締約方所提供之指引，準備一份關於為協助開發中國家締約方（特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中締約方）履行《公約》義務所需資金總額之全面評估報告，以供執行附屬機構於締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之會議審議，並供締約方大會第十八次會議審議；該評估係針對全球環境基金信託基金第十次增資期；</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"(c) 在資源可用的情況下，進一步加強與相關金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，以加速綱要之實施，並著重於改善取得方式；","html":"<p>(c) 在資源可用的情況下，進一步加強與相關金融機構及利害關係人之合作與參與，以加速綱要之實施，並著重於改善取得方式；</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(d) 視適用情況，向於締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之執行附屬機構會議，報告上述子段所述之合作與參與結果，並納入此類參與之選項；","html":"<p>(d) 視適用情況，向於締約方大會第十八次會議前召開之執行附屬機構會議，報告上述子段所述之合作與參與結果，並納入此類參與之選項；</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"(e) 視適用情況，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 子段所述活動之實施。","html":"<p>(e) 視適用情況，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年有效參與上述 (a) 至 (d) 子段所述活動之實施。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"附件 I*\n全球環境基金之額外指引\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書","html":"<p>附件 I*<br />\n全球環境基金之額外指引<br />\n卡塔赫納生物安全議定書</p>","en":[12,13,14]},{"md":"1. **請求**全球環境基金：","html":"<p>1. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金：</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"(a) 為符合資格之締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）提供專門、充足且及時之資金，以建立實施卡塔赫納議定書之法律、行政及其他措施，包括長期強化國家實施能力；","html":"<p>(a) 為符合資格之締約方（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）提供專門、充足且及時之資金，以建立實施卡塔赫納議定書之法律、行政及其他措施，包括長期強化國家實施能力；</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"* 本附件發布時尚未經過正式編輯。","html":"<ul>\n<li>本附件發布時尚未經過正式編輯。</li>\n</ul>","en":[17,18]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p008.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"(b) To continue to provide support for the effective use of the Biosafety Clearing-House, as necessary;"},{"t":"(c) To assist eligible Parties by providing them, sufficiently in advance of the reporting deadline, with financial support to hold adequate national consultations, thus giving them enough time to prepare their sixth national reports and submit them in a timely manner;"},{"t":"(d) To make dedicated, adequate and timely funding available to eligible Parties to implement compliance action plans developed at the request of the Compliance Committee under the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"(e) To continue to support capacity-building and development on biosafety, as part of country-driven projects, including during the ninth replenishment period of its Trust Fund (July 2026−June 2030) and through the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, according to the mandates of the respective Funds, and to strengthen adequate, predictable and dedicated financing for biosafety to contribute to the full and effective implementation of the Cartagena Protocol;"},{"t":"(f)    To continue to explore ways to simplify the process for submitting biosafety project proposals, taking into account the experiences of Parties, with a view to making funding more accessible."},{"t":"Nagoya Protocol on Access and Benefit Sharing"},{"t":"2.     The Global Environment Facility is requested:"},{"t":"(a) To continue to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and the small island developing States among them, and Parties with economies in transition in implementing the Nagoya Protocol, taking into account the outcomes of the second assessment and review, including by supporting the establishment and operationalization of checkpoints, the publication of checkpoint information through the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House and, where appropriate and in accordance with national circumstances, the effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, to encourage the use of global and regional projects and to make funds available to that end;"},{"t":"(b) To make funds available in a timely manner to support eligible Parties in the preparation and submission of their second national reports on the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol, without creating additional reporting requirements, with a view to securing project approval by the end of 2027, as recommended by the Compliance Committee under the Nagoya Protocol;"},{"t":"(c) To ensure that implementing agencies involved in the project to support the preparation and submission of the second national reports on the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol take steps to minimize administrative, procedural and operational delays in order to facilitate the expeditious disbursement of funding;"},{"t":"(d) To continue its efforts to facilitate access by eligible Parties to the resources necessary for the development and implementation of their national frameworks for access and benefit-sharing;"},{"t":"(e) To continue to provide, within its biodiversity focal area, funding for the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol, with adequate, accessible and predictable resources, taking into account the national priorities and needs of eligible Parties, in particular the special needs and conditions of least developed countries and small island developing States;"},{"t":"3.     The Global Environment Facility, its implementing agencies and relevant partners, within their respective mandates, are encouraged to continue efforts to enhance the accessibility, efficiency and timeliness of financial support for the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol, including, as appropriate, by streamlining administrative and operational procedures, facilitating project development and approval processes and minimizing avoidable delays in the disbursement of resources."},{"t":"8/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(b) 視必要情況，繼續為有效利用生物安全資訊交換所提供支持；\n(c) 透過在報告截止日期前充分地提供財務支持，以協助符合條件之締約方進行充分的國家諮商，從而使該等締約方有足夠時間準備其第六次國家報告並及時提交；\n(d) 為符合條件之締約方提供專屬、充分且及時的資金，以執行根據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》下合規委員會要求所制定之合規行動計畫；\n(e) 作為國家主導計畫的一部分，繼續支持生物安全方面之能力建構與發展，包括在其信託基金第九次增資期間（2026年7月－2030年6月）以及透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金，根據各自基金之授權，並強化生物安全方面充分、可預測且專屬的財務，以促進《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之全面且有效執行；\n(f) 考量締約方之經驗，繼續探索簡化提交生物安全計畫提案程序之方法，以期使資金更易於取得。","html":"<p>(b) 視必要情況，繼續為有效利用生物安全資訊交換所提供支持；<br />\n(c) 透過在報告截止日期前充分地提供財務支持，以協助符合條件之締約方進行充分的國家諮商，從而使該等締約方有足夠時間準備其第六次國家報告並及時提交；<br />\n(d) 為符合條件之締約方提供專屬、充分且及時的資金，以執行根據《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》下合規委員會要求所制定之合規行動計畫；<br />\n(e) 作為國家主導計畫的一部分，繼續支持生物安全方面之能力建構與發展，包括在其信託基金第九次增資期間（2026年7月－2030年6月）以及透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金，根據各自基金之授權，並強化生物安全方面充分、可預測且專屬的財務，以促進《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》之全面且有效執行；<br />\n(f) 考量締約方之經驗，繼續探索簡化提交生物安全計畫提案程序之方法，以期使資金更易於取得。</p>","en":[2,3,4,5]},{"md":"關於取得與利益分享之名古屋議定書","html":"<p>關於取得與利益分享之名古屋議定書</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"2.","html":"<p>2.</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"**請求**全球環境基金：","html":"<p><strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金：</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(a) 考量第二次評估與審查之結果，繼續協助開發中國家締約方，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方執行《名古屋議定書》，包括透過支持檢查點之建立與運作、透過取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布檢查點資訊，以及在適當且符合國家情況之情況下，確保原住民族與地方社區之有效參與，以鼓勵全球與區域性計畫之利用，並為此目的提供資金；\n(b) 根據《名古屋議定書》下合規委員會之建議，及時提供資金以支持符合條件之締約方編製並提交其關於執行《名古屋議定書》之第二次國家報告，且不增加額外之報告要求，其目標是在2027年底前確保計畫獲得批准；\n(c) 確保參與支持編製與提交《名古屋議定書》執行第二次國家報告計畫之執行機構，採取措施以減少行政、程序與作業上之延遲，以促進資金之迅速撥付；\n(d) 繼續致力於促進符合條件之締約方取得開發與執行其取得與利益分享國家框架所需之資源；\n(e) 在其生物多樣性核心領域內，考量符合條件之締約方之國家優先事項與需求，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家之特殊需求與條件，繼續提供充分、易於取得且可預測之資源，用於執行《名古屋議定書》；","html":"<p>(a) 考量第二次評估與審查之結果，繼續協助開發中國家締約方，特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方執行《名古屋議定書》，包括透過支持檢查點之建立與運作、透過取得與利益分享資訊交換所發布檢查點資訊，以及在適當且符合國家情況之情況下，確保原住民族與地方社區之有效參與，以鼓勵全球與區域性計畫之利用，並為此目的提供資金；<br />\n(b) 根據《名古屋議定書》下合規委員會之建議，及時提供資金以支持符合條件之締約方編製並提交其關於執行《名古屋議定書》之第二次國家報告，且不增加額外之報告要求，其目標是在2027年底前確保計畫獲得批准；<br />\n(c) 確保參與支持編製與提交《名古屋議定書》執行第二次國家報告計畫之執行機構，採取措施以減少行政、程序與作業上之延遲，以促進資金之迅速撥付；<br />\n(d) 繼續致力於促進符合條件之締約方取得開發與執行其取得與利益分享國家框架所需之資源；<br />\n(e) 在其生物多樣性核心領域內，考量符合條件之締約方之國家優先事項與需求，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家之特殊需求與條件，繼續提供充分、易於取得且可預測之資源，用於執行《名古屋議定書》；</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"3.","html":"<p>3.</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"**鼓勵**全球環境基金、其執行機構及相關夥伴在其各自之授權範圍內，繼續致力於提升執行《名古屋議定書》財務支持之易取得性、效率與及時性，包括在適當情況下，透過精簡行政與作業程序、促進計畫開發與批准程序，以及減少資源撥付中可避免之延遲。","html":"<p><strong>鼓勵</strong>全球環境基金、其執行機構及相關夥伴在其各自之授權範圍內，繼續致力於提升執行《名古屋議定書》財務支持之易取得性、效率與及時性，包括在適當情況下，透過精簡行政與作業程序、促進計畫開發與批准程序，以及減少資源撥付中可避免之延遲。</p>","en":[13]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p009.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"Biodiversity and health"},{"t":"4.     The Global Environmental Facility is requested to provide financial support for the implementation of the Global Action Plan, according to its mandate."},{"t":"Synthetic biology"},{"t":"5.      The Global Environment Facility is requested, and other donors are invited, to make available financial resources to developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small islands developing States, and countries with economies in transition to support the implementation of the thematic action plan, in accordance with national needs and priorities, including for strengthening national capacities for horizon scanning, monitoring and assessment, environmental risk assessment, risk management and regulatory oversight."},{"t":"Gender Plan of Action"},{"t":"6.     Relevant international financial institutions are invited and the Global Environment Facility is requested to support gender-responsive biodiversity actions and improve processes related to access to funding, including through simplified access modalities, for women-led initiatives, including from indigenous peoples and local communities, in accordance with their respective mandates."},{"t":"Capacity-building and development and technical and scientific cooperation"},{"t":"7.    The request made in paragraph 23 of decision 16/3 to the Global Environment Facility, including through the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, is reiterated, and other relevant multilateral funds and international financial institutions, in accordance with their mandates, are invited to continue to support in all eligible countries country-driven projects that include technical and scientific cooperation, technology transfer and capacity-building for the implementation of the Framework."},{"t":"8.     The request made in paragraph 24 of decision 16/3 to the Global Environment Facility, including through the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, is reiterated and other relevant multilateral funds and international financial institutions, in accordance with their mandates, are invited to support the operationalization and activities of the technical and scientific cooperation support centres in developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States among them, and Parties with economies in transition, as appropriate, in response to their requests in their respective subregions, in the context of country-driven projects of the eligible countries."},{"t":"Planning, monitoring, reporting and review"},{"t":"9.     The Global Environment Facility and its implementing agencies are requested, before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, to put in place any procedures or organizational arrangements necessary to ensure that timely, adequate and accessible resources, including the disbursement of funds to recipient countries well in advance of the reporting deadline, are provided for the eighth round of national reporting, including support for making use of the headline indicators in the monitoring framework for the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, and to initiate such support in a timely and accelerated manner and in a way that supports country ownership and the early engagement of relevant national authorities. Global review of collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework"},{"t":"10. The Global Environment Facility is requested to enhance the provision of adequate, predictable, timely and transparent means of implementation in an easily accessible manner to developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and the small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, including by simplifying access procedures and strengthening country ownership of activities to support the Framework, in"},{"t":"9/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"生物多樣性與健康\n4. **請求**全球環境基金根據其職權，為全球行動計畫的實施提供財務支持。","html":"<p>生物多樣性與健康<br />\n4. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金根據其職權，為全球行動計畫的實施提供財務支持。</p>","en":[2,3]},{"md":"合成生物學\n5. **請求**全球環境基金並**邀請**其他捐助者，根據國家需求與優先事項，提供財務資源予開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中之國家，以支持主題行動計畫之實施，包括強化針對前瞻性掃描、監測與評估、環境風險評估、風險管理及監管監督之國家能力。","html":"<p>合成生物學<br />\n5. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金並<strong>邀請</strong>其他捐助者，根據國家需求與優先事項，提供財務資源予開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中之國家，以支持主題行動計畫之實施，包括強化針對前瞻性掃描、監測與評估、環境風險評估、風險管理及監管監督之國家能力。</p>","en":[4,5]},{"md":"性別行動計畫\n6. **邀請**相關國際金融機構並**請求**全球環境基金，根據其各自職權，支持具性別回應性之生物多樣性行動，並改善與取得資金相關之程序（包括透過簡化之取得模式），以支持由女性主導之倡議，包括來自原住民族與地方社區之倡議。","html":"<p>性別行動計畫<br />\n6. <strong>邀請</strong>相關國際金融機構並<strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金，根據其各自職權，支持具性別回應性之生物多樣性行動，並改善與取得資金相關之程序（包括透過簡化之取得模式），以支持由女性主導之倡議，包括來自原住民族與地方社區之倡議。</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"能力建構與發展及技術與科學合作\n7. 重申決議 16/3 第 23 段向全球環境基金（包括透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金）所提出之請求，並**邀請**其他相關多邊基金與國際金融機構根據其職權，繼續在所有合資格國家中，支持包含技術與科學合作、技術轉移及能力建構之由國家主導計畫，以實施本綱要。\n8. 重申決議 16/3 第 24 段向全球環境基金（包括透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金）所提出之請求，並**邀請**其他相關多邊基金與國際金融機構根據其職權，在合資格國家之國家主導計畫脈絡下，針對其各自次區域內所提出之請求，視情況支持開發中國家締約方（特別是其中之低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及經濟轉型中之締約方，其技術與科學合作支援中心之運作與活動。","html":"<p>能力建構與發展及技術與科學合作<br />\n7. 重申決議 16/3 第 23 段向全球環境基金（包括透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金）所提出之請求，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他相關多邊基金與國際金融機構根據其職權，繼續在所有合資格國家中，支持包含技術與科學合作、技術轉移及能力建構之由國家主導計畫，以實施本綱要。<br />\n8. 重申決議 16/3 第 24 段向全球環境基金（包括透過全球生物多樣性綱要基金）所提出之請求，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他相關多邊基金與國際金融機構根據其職權，在合資格國家之國家主導計畫脈絡下，針對其各自次區域內所提出之請求，視情況支持開發中國家締約方（特別是其中之低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）以及經濟轉型中之締約方，其技術與科學合作支援中心之運作與活動。</p>","en":[8,9,10]},{"md":"規劃、監測、報告與審查\n9. **請求**全球環境基金及其執行機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前，建立任何必要之程序或組織安排，以確保第八輪國家報告能獲得及時、充足且可取得之資源，包括在報告截止日期前充分撥付資金予受援國，包括支持利用昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構中之主要指標，並以及時、加速且支持國家自主權及相關國家主管機關早期參與之方式，啟動此類支持。","html":"<p>規劃、監測、報告與審查<br />\n9. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金及其執行機構在第十八次締約方大會召開前，建立任何必要之程序或組織安排，以確保第八輪國家報告能獲得及時、充足且可取得之資源，包括在報告截止日期前充分撥付資金予受援國，包括支持利用昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構中之主要指標，並以及時、加速且支持國家自主權及相關國家主管機關早期參與之方式，啟動此類支持。</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"全球審查實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之集體進展\n10. **請求**全球環境基金強化提供充足、可預測、及時且透明之實施手段，並以易於取得之方式提供予開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中之締約方，包括透過簡化取得程序及強化對支持本綱要活動之國家自主權。","html":"<p>全球審查實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之集體進展<br />\n10. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金強化提供充足、可預測、及時且透明之實施手段，並以易於取得之方式提供予開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家、小島嶼開發中國家以及經濟轉型中之締約方，包括透過簡化取得程序及強化對支持本綱要活動之國家自主權。</p>","en":[12,13]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p010.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"accordance with national biodiversity strategies and action plans, and to share through existing reporting arrangements, and without creating additional burdens, detailed information on the resources provided and how they address the needs and priorities identified by Parties through their projects, without prejudice to the process established under decision[s] 16/34 of 27 February 2025 [and 17/--] on resource mobilization."},{"t":"11. The Global Environment Facility and its implementing agencies, including the United Nations Development Programme in the context of the Biodiversity Finance Initiative, are requested to expedite the support to all eligible Parties on their enabling support activities for the development of biodiversity finance plans, in order to unlock financial resources for the implementation of national biodiversity strategies and action plans, as described in decision 15/7 of 19 December 2022."},{"t":"12. The Global Environment Facility is requested to continue to support the development and strengthening of national monitoring and knowledge management systems, including national ecosystem data and spatial information, inter alia, to enable the operationalization of the ecosystem-based headline indicators."},{"t":"Resource mobilization"},{"t":"13. The Global Environment Facility is requested, and other relevant existing financial entities, including international financial institutions and multilateral development banks, are invited, to take into account the criteria adopted in decision 17/--, as appropriate, in their ongoing efforts to reform or improve their operations."},{"t":"Annex II"},{"t":"Terms of reference for a full assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034)"},{"t":"A.     Objective and scope"},{"t":"1.    The objective of the work to be carried out under the present terms of reference is to enable the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity12 to make an assessment of the amount of funds that are necessary to assist developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition, in accordance with the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties, in fulfilling their commitments under the Convention and its Protocols, in particular the commitment to implementing any successor to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework 13 over the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund (July 2030–June 2034), and determine the amount of resources needed, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention and decision III/8 of 15 November 1996 of the Conference of the Parties."},{"t":"B.     Methodology"},{"t":"2.     The funding needs assessment should be conducted taking into account:"},{"t":"(a)     Article 20 and paragraph 1 of Article 21 of the Convention, as well as the Framework;"},{"t":"(b) Guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties, which may call for future financial resources, and in the resource mobilization decision, in which the Conference of the Parties calls for a broadening of the contributor base;"},{"t":"12 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"13 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"10/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"根據國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，並透過現有的報告安排進行分享，且在不增加額外負擔的情況下，提供關於所提供資源之詳細資訊，以及這些資源如何透過其專案來應對締約方所識別的需求與優先事項，且不損害根據 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議[s] 16/34 [及 17/--] 就資源動員所建立之程序。","html":"<p>根據國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫，並透過現有的報告安排進行分享，且在不增加額外負擔的情況下，提供關於所提供資源之詳細資訊，以及這些資源如何透過其專案來應對締約方所識別的需求與優先事項，且不損害根據 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議[s] 16/34 [及 17/--] 就資源動員所建立之程序。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"11. **請求**全球環境基金及其執行機構，包括聯合國開發計畫在生物多樣性融資倡議背景下之角色，加速對所有符合資格締約方在開發生物多樣性融資計畫之啟動支援活動方面提供支援，以釋放用於執行國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之財務資源，如 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/7 所述。","html":"<p>11. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金及其執行機構，包括聯合國開發計畫在生物多樣性融資倡議背景下之角色，加速對所有符合資格締約方在開發生物多樣性融資計畫之啟動支援活動方面提供支援，以釋放用於執行國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫之財務資源，如 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/7 所述。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"12. **請求**全球環境基金繼續支援國家監測與知識管理系統之開發與強化，包括國家生態系資料與空間資訊，其中包括為了使以生態系為基礎的主要指標得以運作。","html":"<p>12. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金繼續支援國家監測與知識管理系統之開發與強化，包括國家生態系資料與空間資訊，其中包括為了使以生態系為基礎的主要指標得以運作。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"資源動員","html":"<p>資源動員</p>","pre":"使以生態系為基礎的主要指標得以運作。\n\n","en":[4]},{"md":"13. **請求**全球環境基金，並**邀請**其他相關之現有財務實體，包括國際金融機構與多邊開發銀行，在改進或改善其運作之持續努力中，視情況考慮決議 17/-- 中所採納之標準。","html":"<p>13. <strong>請求</strong>全球環境基金，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他相關之現有財務實體，包括國際金融機構與多邊開發銀行，在改進或改善其運作之持續努力中，視情況考慮決議 17/-- 中所採納之標準。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"附件 II\n關於全面評估所需資金金額之任務說明書，旨在根據締約方所提供之指引，協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方，在全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在《公約》下之承諾。","html":"<p>附件 II<br />\n關於全面評估所需資金金額之任務說明書，旨在根據締約方所提供之指引，協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方，在全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）履行其在《公約》下之承諾。</p>","en":[6,7]},{"md":"A.\n目標與範圍","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標與範圍</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1.\n本任務說明書下所執行工作之目標，是為了使生物多樣性公約締約方會議¹²能夠進行評估，以確定在履行其於《公約》及其議定書下之承諾時，特別是履行於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）內，執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要¹³ 之任何後續綱要之承諾時，協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方，所需之資金金額，並根據《公約》第 21 條第 1 段及締約方大會 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8，確定所需資源之金額。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n本任務說明書下所執行工作之目標，是為了使生物多樣性公約締約方會議¹²能夠進行評估，以確定在履行其於《公約》及其議定書下之承諾時，特別是履行於全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間（2030 年 7 月至 2034 年 6 月）內，執行昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要¹³ 之任何後續綱要之承諾時，協助開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方，所需之資金金額，並根據《公約》第 21 條第 1 段及締約方大會 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8，確定所需資源之金額。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"B.\n方法論","html":"<p>B.<br />\n方法論</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"2.\n資金需求評估應考慮以下因素：\n(a) 《公約》第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及《綱要》；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n資金需求評估應考慮以下因素：<br />\n(a) 《公約》第 20 條及第 21 條第 1 段，以及《綱要》；</p>","en":[11,12]},{"md":"(b) 締約方大會向財務機制提供之指引，該指引可能要求未來之財務資源，以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中；","html":"<p>(b) 締約方大會向財務機制提供之指引，該指引可能要求未來之財務資源，以及在要求擴大捐助者基礎之資源動員決議中；</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"---\n¹² 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n¹³ 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹² 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n¹³ 決議 15/4，附件。</p>","en":[14,15,16]}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p011.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"(c) All obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and relevant decisions adopted by the Conference of the Parties, in particular the Framework;"},{"t":"(d) National strategies, plans or programmes developed in accordance with Article 6 of the Convention and national biodiversity finance plans or similar instruments, where available;"},{"t":"(e) Information communicated to the Conference of the Parties in national reports and by the Parties through the financial reporting framework and other submission responses to surveys and interviews;"},{"t":"(f)   Policies and guidelines agreed by the Council of the Global Environment Facility for determining eligibility for funding of projects;"},{"t":"(g) Synergies with other biodiversity-related conventions and other multilateral environmental agreements funded by the Global Environment Facility, including those with respect to operations and impacts;"},{"t":"(h) Additional private capital mobilized through blended finance, including through the use of non-grant instruments, while recognizing the challenges that may be experienced by some Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, in mobilizing private capital in this regard;"},{"t":"(i)     Policy coherence;"},{"t":"(j)   Other relevant estimations, including the costs of implementing the Gender Plan of Action (2023–2030);14"},{"t":"(k) Exchange rates, inflation and the incremental costs of the implementation of the provisions of the Convention in developing countries."},{"t":"3.    In the context of the assessment, interviews, surveys, quantitative and qualitative analyses, and consultations should be undertaken, as needed for the preparation of the report, including:"},{"t":"(a) A compilation and analysis of the needs identified in national biodiversity strategies and action plans and national biodiversity finance plans, including country-specific resource mobilization strategies, prepared by Global Environment Facility-eligible and other relevant Parties pursuant to Article 6 of the Convention, taking into account incremental cost funding as the fundamental operational principle of the Global Environment Facility;"},{"t":"(b) A review of reports submitted by Parties pursuant to Articles 6 and 26 of the Convention, as well as Article 33 of the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety15 and Article 29 of the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization, 16 to identify funding needs related to the fulfilment of their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(c) The estimated financial implications of guidance provided to the financial mechanism by the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(d) A compilation and analysis of any supplementary information provided by Global Environment Facility-eligible Parties on their funding needs for the implementation of their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols."},{"t":"C.      Implementation"},{"t":"4.    The national focal points of the Convention and the focal points of the financial mechanism should, as appropriate, bear joint responsibility for coordinating national-level incremental funding"},{"t":"14 Decision 15/11, annex."},{"t":"15 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 2226, No. 30619."},{"t":"16 Ibid., vol. 3008, No. 30619"},{"t":"11/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"(c) 公約及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是《綱要》；\n(d) 根據公約第六條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；\n(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會提交之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定計畫資助資格之政策與指南；\n(g) 與其他與生物多樣性相關之公約，以及由全球環境基金資助之其他多邊環境協議之協同效應，包括在運作與影響方面之協同效應；\n(h) 透過混合金融（包括透過使用非撥款工具）所動員之額外私人資本，同時承認某些締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在於此方面動員私人資本時可能面臨的挑戰；\n(i) 政策一致性；\n(j) 其他相關估算，包括實施性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；¹⁴\n(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹，以及在開發中國家實施公約條款之增量成本。","html":"<p>(c) 公約及其議定書下之所有義務，以及締約方大會所通過之相關決議，特別是《綱要》；<br />\n(d) 根據公約第六條所制定之國家策略、計畫或方案，以及國家生物多樣性財務計畫或類似工具（若有）；<br />\n(e) 透過國家報告向締約方大會提交之資訊，以及締約方透過財務報告架構及對調查與訪談之其他提交回應所提供之資訊；<br />\n(f) 全球環境基金理事會所同意，用於判定計畫資助資格之政策與指南；<br />\n(g) 與其他與生物多樣性相關之公約，以及由全球環境基金資助之其他多邊環境協議之協同效應，包括在運作與影響方面之協同效應；<br />\n(h) 透過混合金融（包括透過使用非撥款工具）所動員之額外私人資本，同時承認某些締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，在於此方面動員私人資本時可能面臨的挑戰；<br />\n(i) 政策一致性；<br />\n(j) 其他相關估算，包括實施性別行動計畫（2023–2030）之成本；¹⁴<br />\n(k) 匯率、通貨膨脹，以及在開發中國家實施公約條款之增量成本。</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"3.\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮詢，包括：\n(a) 彙編並分析國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括由符合全球環境基金資格之締約方及其他相關締約方根據公約第六條所編製之特定國家資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；\n(b) 審查締約方根據公約第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第33條¹⁵與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》第29條¹⁶所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在公約及其議定書下之義務相關的資金需求；\n(c) 估算締約方向財務機制提供之指引所產生的財務影響；\n(d) 彙編並分析符合全球環境基金資格之締約方，就履行其在公約及其議定書下之義務所需之資金需求所提供之任何補充資訊。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在評估脈絡下，應根據編製報告之需要，進行訪談、調查、定量與定性分析及諮詢，包括：<br />\n(a) 彙編並分析國家生物多樣性策略與行動計畫及國家生物多樣性財務計畫中所識別之需求，包括由符合全球環境基金資格之締約方及其他相關締約方根據公約第六條所編製之特定國家資源動員策略，並應將增量成本資助視為全球環境基金之基本運作原則；<br />\n(b) 審查締約方根據公約第六條與第二十六條，以及《卡塔赫納生物安全議定書》第33條¹⁵與《取得遺傳資源並公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書》第29條¹⁶所提交之報告，以識別與履行其在公約及其議定書下之義務相關的資金需求；<br />\n(c) 估算締約方向財務機制提供之指引所產生的財務影響；<br />\n(d) 彙編並分析符合全球環境基金資格之締約方，就履行其在公約及其議定書下之義務所需之資金需求所提供之任何補充資訊。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"C. 實施","html":"<p>C. 實施</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"4.\n公約之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點，應視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資金","html":"<p>4.<br />\n公約之國家聯絡點與財務機制之聯絡點，應視情況共同負責協調國家層級之增量資金</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"---\n¹⁴ 決議 15/11，附件。\n¹⁵ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。\n¹⁶ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹⁴ 決議 15/11，附件。<br />\n¹⁵ 聯合國，條約集，第 2226 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n¹⁶ 同上，第 3008 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[17,18,19]},{"md":"11/15","html":"<p>11/15</p>","en":[20]}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p012.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"needs assessments, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders and other focal points under the Convention and related conventions to ensure a whole-of-government approach."},{"t":"5.    The national focal points may establish a national platform or use existing national coordination mechanisms, or both, to aid project planning, as necessary, and track ongoing biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities. Close links should be established between the national platform or relevant coordination mechanism and national support initiatives of relevant funding providers, in particular the country engagement strategy of the Global Environment Facility."},{"t":"6.    The national platform should also facilitate the participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women’s and youth organizations and other relevant stakeholders, taking into account section C of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, as appropriate, subject to national legislation."},{"t":"7.     The Executive Secretary should provide the information received from Parties without additional reporting obligations on funding needs through an online platform, subject to the availability of resources, to facilitate the visualization of biodiversity funding needs, gaps and priorities on an ongoing basis."},{"t":"8.     The Executive Secretary should prepare a report on the full assessment, and the report should be submitted for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties, with a view to providing recommendations for consideration by the Conference of the Parties at that meeting."},{"t":"9.    At its eighteenth meeting, the Conference of the Parties will be invited to take note of the estimated amount of funds that are necessary for the implementation of the Convention and its Protocols for the tenth replenishment period of the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund."},{"t":"Annex III"},{"t":"Terms of reference for the seventh quadrennial review"},{"t":"of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism"},{"t":"A.     Objectives"},{"t":"1.    In accordance with paragraph 3 of Article 21 of the Convention on Biological Diversity17 and building upon the experience of the past six reviews of the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, the Conference of the Parties to the Convention will undertake its seventh review at its eighteenth meeting and take appropriate action to improve the effectiveness of the financial mechanism, as necessary. For that purpose, the following elements will be included in the review:"},{"t":"(a) The conformity of the activities of the Global Environment Facility, as the institutional structure operating the financial mechanism, with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(b) The effectiveness of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources to enable eligible developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition to meet the agreed full incremental costs to them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits, and benefit from their provisions, taking into account the need for predictability, adequacy, accessibility and timely flow of funds, including the performance of the Global Environment Facility implementing agencies;"},{"t":"(c) The efficiency of the financial mechanism in providing financial resources and, in accordance with the guidance of the Conference of the Parties, overseeing, monitoring and evaluating the results of activities financed by its resources, including their social and gender- and equity-related outcomes and impacts, as relevant;"},{"t":"17 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"12/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"需求評估，並與相關利害關係人及《公約》與相關公約下的其他焦點聯繫點合作，以確保採取全政府方法。","html":"<p>需求評估，並與相關利害關係人及《公約》與相關公約下的其他焦點聯繫點合作，以確保採取全政府方法。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"5.\n國家焦點聯繫點可視需要建立國家平台或利用現有的國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助專案規劃，並追蹤持續性的生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。國家平台或相關協調機制，應與相關出資者之國家支持倡議建立緊密聯繫，特別是全球環境基金的國家參與策略。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n國家焦點聯繫點可視需要建立國家平台或利用現有的國家協調機制，或兩者兼具，以協助專案規劃，並追蹤持續性的生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項。國家平台或相關協調機制，應與相關出資者之國家支持倡議建立緊密聯繫，特別是全球環境基金的國家參與策略。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"6.\n國家平台亦應在符合國家立法且適當的情況下，考量《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》C 節，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n國家平台亦應在符合國家立法且適當的情況下，考量《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》C 節，促進原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年組織及其他相關利害關係人之參與。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"7.\n在資源可及的情況下，執行秘書應透過線上平台提供從締約方收到的資訊，且不增加關於資金需求的額外報告義務，以促進生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項的持續視覺化。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n在資源可及的情況下，執行秘書應透過線上平台提供從締約方收到的資訊，且不增加關於資金需求的額外報告義務，以促進生物多樣性資金需求、缺口與優先事項的持續視覺化。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"8.\n執行秘書應針對完整評估編製一份報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構，於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，旨在為該次締約方大會提供供其審議之建議。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n執行秘書應針對完整評估編製一份報告，且該報告應提交予執行附屬機構，於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議，旨在為該次締約方大會提供供其審議之建議。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"9.\n在第十八次會議期間，將邀請締約方大會注意到，為全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間，執行《公約》及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n在第十八次會議期間，將邀請締約方大會注意到，為全球環境基金信託基金第十期增資期間，執行《公約》及其議定書所需之估算資金金額。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"附件 III\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍","html":"<p>附件 III<br />\n財務機制有效性第七次四年一度審查之職權範圍</p>","en":[7,8,9]},{"md":"A.\n目標","html":"<p>A.<br />\n目標</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"1.\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第 21 條第 3 項¹⁷，並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，本公約締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提高財務機制的有效性。為此，審查將包含下列要素：\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動與締約方大會指引之符合性；\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使符合條件的開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，能夠支付其透過執行措施以履行《公約》及其議定書下之義務，且該等措施能產生全球環境效益並從其規定中獲益之所達成之約定全額增量成本，並考量資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，且根據締約方大會之指引，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；","html":"<p>1.<br />\n根據《生物多樣性公約》第 21 條第 3 項¹⁷，並基於過去六次財務機制有效性審查之經驗，本公約締約方大會將於其第十八次會議進行第七次審查，並於必要時採取適當行動以提高財務機制的有效性。為此，審查將包含下列要素：<br />\n(a) 作為運作財務機制之制度結構，全球環境基金之活動與締約方大會指引之符合性；<br />\n(b) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之有效性，以使符合條件的開發中國家締約方，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中締約方，能夠支付其透過執行措施以履行《公約》及其議定書下之義務，且該等措施能產生全球環境效益並從其規定中獲益之所達成之約定全額增量成本，並考量資金之可預測性、充足性、可取得性及時流動之需求，包括全球環境基金執行機構之績效；<br />\n(c) 財務機制在提供財務資源方面之效率，且根據締約方大會之指引，對其資源所資助之活動結果進行監督、監測與評估，包括其相關之社會、性別及公平相關之成果與影響；</p>","en":[11,12,13,14]},{"md":"¹⁷ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p>¹⁷ 聯合國，《聯合國條約集》，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[15,16]}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p013.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"(d) The effectiveness of catalysing and enhancing national implementation measures in line with national priorities for achieving global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(e) The efficiency and effectiveness of the activities funded by the Global Environment Facility and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund for the implementation of the Convention and the achievement of its three objectives, as well as, as applicable, the implementation of its Protocols, taking into account the guidance provided by the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(f)   The efficiency and effectiveness of processes and procedures for the deployment and use of resources, including simplified procedures and access modalities;"},{"t":"(g) The effectiveness and efficiency of the support provided for the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols in synergy with the implementation of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, in a manner that is consistent with the mandates of the respective agreements;"},{"t":"(h) The effectiveness in improving access to financial resources and trends associated with funding for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth to support the implementation of the objectives of the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(i)    The efficiency of each of the implementing agencies of the Global Environment Facility in providing technical support and services to countries in their preparation of project proposals and the implementation of projects, including with regard to the timely disbursement of fund, fees and project management costs, use of international consultants and control of expenditure."},{"t":"B.     Methodology"},{"t":"2.   The review will cover all the activities of the institutional structure operating the financial mechanism, in particular for the period from 1 July 2022 to 30 June 2026."},{"t":"3.    The review shall draw upon, inter alia, and in a balanced manner, the following sources of information:"},{"t":"(a) The reviews of effectiveness of the financial mechanism in implementing the Convention undertaken pursuant to the memorandum of understanding between the Conference of the Parties to the Convention and the Council of the Global Environment Facility, as contained in the annex to decision III/8 of 15 November 1996;"},{"t":"(b) Reports prepared by the Global Environment Facility, including its reports for meetings of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention;"},{"t":"(c) Reports of the Independent Evaluation Office of the Global Environment Facility that relate to the biodiversity-related activities of the Facility, including the eighth comprehensive evaluation of the Global Environment Facility, as well as relevant assessments by the agencies accredited by the Council of the Facility and other partners;"},{"t":"(d) The Multilateral Performance Network 18 assessments of the Global Environment Facility and relevant reports related to the review of the vertical climate and environmental funds;"},{"t":"(e) Information regarding the financial mechanism provided by Parties through national reports and other submissions, surveys and interviews;"},{"t":"(f)   Information provided by indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and relevant stakeholders related to projects funded through the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, including their views on possible impacts on their rights, as applicable, as well as documented evidence and assessments of such impacts, including gender-differentiated impacts;"},{"t":"18 See www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html."},{"t":"13/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(d) 根據國家優先事項，催化並強化國家執行措施之成效，以達成全球生物多樣性目標與標靶，包括與本公約及其議定書相關之目標；\n(e) 考量締約方大會所提供之指引，由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於執行本公約、達成其三大目標，以及（在適用情況下）執行其議定書之活動的效率與成效；\n(f) 資源部署與使用之程序與流程的效率與成效，包括簡化程序與取得模式；\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之執行產生綜效，且與各自協議之授權一致之情況下，為達成本公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持的成效與效率；\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之成效，以及與資助原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年以支持執行本公約及其議定書目標相關之趨勢；\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在為各國提供技術支持與服務（包括協助其編製計畫提案與執行計畫）方面的效率，包括有關資金、費用與計畫管理成本的及時撥付、國際顧問的使用以及支出控制之情況。","html":"<p>(d) 根據國家優先事項，催化並強化國家執行措施之成效，以達成全球生物多樣性目標與標靶，包括與本公約及其議定書相關之目標；<br />\n(e) 考量締約方大會所提供之指引，由全球環境基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助，用於執行本公約、達成其三大目標，以及（在適用情況下）執行其議定書之活動的效率與成效；<br />\n(f) 資源部署與使用之程序與流程的效率與成效，包括簡化程序與取得模式；<br />\n(g) 在與其他相關多邊環境協議之執行產生綜效，且與各自協議之授權一致之情況下，為達成本公約及其議定書目標所提供之支持的成效與效率；<br />\n(h) 改善取得財務資源之成效，以及與資助原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年以支持執行本公約及其議定書目標相關之趨勢；<br />\n(i) 全球環境基金各執行機構在為各國提供技術支持與服務（包括協助其編製計畫提案與執行計畫）方面的效率，包括有關資金、費用與計畫管理成本的及時撥付、國際顧問的使用以及支出控制之情況。</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"方法論","html":"<p>方法論</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"2.\n本次審查將涵蓋運作財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是針對 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。\n3.\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據本公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄，所進行之關於財務機制在執行本公約成效之審查；\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為本公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；\n(d) 多邊績效網絡 (Multilateral Performance Network)¹⁸ 對全球環境基金之評估，以及與審查垂直氣候與環境基金相關之報告；\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，關於透過全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關資訊，包括（在適用情況下）其對自身權利可能產生影響之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；","html":"<p>2.<br />\n本次審查將涵蓋運作財務機制之制度結構的所有活動，特別是針對 2022 年 7 月 1 日至 2026 年 6 月 30 日期間。<br />\n3.<br />\n審查應以平衡方式，除其他外，利用下列資訊來源：<br />\n(a) 根據 1996 年 11 月 15 日決議 III/8 附件所載，依據本公約締約方大會與全球環境基金理事會間之合作備忘錄，所進行之關於財務機制在執行本公約成效之審查；<br />\n(b) 由全球環境基金編製之報告，包括其為本公約締約方大會會議所編製之報告；<br />\n(c) 全球環境基金獨立評估辦公室與基金生物多樣性相關活動有關之報告，包括全球環境基金第八次全面評估，以及由基金理事會認可之機構及其他合作夥伴所進行之相關評估；<br />\n(d) 多邊績效網絡 (Multilateral Performance Network)¹⁸ 對全球環境基金之評估，以及與審查垂直氣候與環境基金相關之報告；<br />\n(e) 締約方透過國家報告及其他提交文件、調查與訪談所提供關於財務機制之資訊；<br />\n(f) 由原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及相關利害關係人所提供，關於透過全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金資助之計畫相關資訊，包括（在適用情況下）其對自身權利可能產生影響之看法，以及此類影響（包括性別差異化影響）之文件證據與評估；</p>","en":[8,9,10,11,12]},{"md":"¹⁸ 參見 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。","html":"<p>¹⁸ 參見 www.mopan.org/en/our-work/performance-evidence/gef.html。</p>","en":[13,14,15,16]},{"md":"13/15","html":"<p>13/15</p>","en":[17]}]},{"p":"p014","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p014.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"(g)     Experience with, and lessons learned from, relevant international financial mechanisms;"},{"t":"(h) The report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(i)   The stocktake review of the operations and performance of the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund regarding its scale, speed and accessibility and the future arrangements requested in decision 15/15 of 19 December 2022."},{"t":"C.     Criteria"},{"t":"4.   The effectiveness and efficiency of the financial mechanism should be assessed taking into account, inter alia:"},{"t":"(a) The actions taken by the Global Environment Facility in response to the guidance of the Conference of the Parties and to the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework,19 including through the decisions of the Global Environment Facility Council on relations with conventions and international institutions;"},{"t":"(b) The extent to which [all] eligible Parties[, including developing countries, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States, and Parties with economies in transition] take measures to apply for and receive timely, adequate and predictable funding to enable them to meet the agreed full incremental cost to them of implementing measures through which they fulfil their obligations under the Convention and its Protocols and that generate global environmental benefits;"},{"t":"(c) Information provided by Parties in relation to their performance in delivering projects, such as constraints affecting those Parties, as well as women and youth, under the Global Environment Facility Trust Fund and the Global Biodiversity Framework Fund, and on the performance of implementing agencies;"},{"t":"(d) Percentage of eligible Parties that have received financial support from the financial mechanism for implementing global biodiversity goals and targets, including those related to the Convention and its Protocols;"},{"t":"(e) Percentage of biodiversity-relevant funding through the financial mechanism in support of the achievement of global biodiversity goals and targets;"},{"t":"(f)   Trends in co-financing, in particular private and non-grant financing in the biodiversity focal area enabled by the financial mechanism;"},{"t":"(g) Trends in financing global, regional and subregional biodiversity projects under the financial mechanism;"},{"t":"(h) Trends in financing that take into consideration synergies among conventions for which the Global Environment Facility has been designated to operate their financial mechanism on an ongoing and interim basis;"},{"t":"(i)   Trends in financing targeted at biodiversity-related conventions and agreements taking into consideration synergies among them;"},{"t":"(j)   Trends in time frames for project development and resource disbursement, including the time between the project approval and the first disbursement;"},{"t":"(k) Trends in financing targeted at or led by indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, including progress on modalities of access to finance;"},{"t":"(l)    Trends in the number and themes of capacity-building activities that enable Parties and stakeholders to secure access to financing from the Global Environment Facility;"},{"t":"19 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"14/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"(g)\n與相關國際財務機制之經驗及從中學習到的教訓；","html":"<p>(g)<br />\n與相關國際財務機制之經驗及從中學習到的教訓；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"(h) 全球環境基金理事會針對第十七次締約方大會所提交之報告；\n(i) 針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之規模、速度與可取得性，以及根據 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排，進行其運作與績效之盤點審查。","html":"<p>(h) 全球環境基金理事會針對第十七次締約方大會所提交之報告；<br />\n(i) 針對全球生物多樣性綱要基金之規模、速度與可取得性，以及根據 2022 年 12 月 19 日決議 15/15 所要求之未來安排，進行其運作與績效之盤點審查。</p>","en":[2,3]},{"md":"C.\n標準","html":"<p>C.<br />\n標準</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"4.\n財務機制之有效性與效率應在考量下列事項時進行評估，其中包括：\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之指引所採取之行動，<sup>19</sup> 包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議所採取之行動；\n(b) [所有] 合格締約方[，包括開發中國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方] 採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書下義務、並產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本之程度；\n(c) 締約方所提供關於其執行全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下專案績效之資訊，例如影響該等締約方以及女性與青年的限制因素，以及執行機構之績效；\n(d) 合格締約方中，透過財務機制獲得財務支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；\n(h) 考量到全球環境基金已被指定以持續及臨時方式運作其財務機制之各公約間綜效，其資助趨勢；\n(i) 考量到生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效，針對該等公約與協議之資助趨勢；\n(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括專案核准至首次撥款之間的時間；\n(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之資助趨勢，包括取得資金模式之進展；\n(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠確保取得全球環境基金資金之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；","html":"<p>4.<br />\n財務機制之有效性與效率應在考量下列事項時進行評估，其中包括：<br />\n(a) 全球環境基金因應締約方大會及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之指引所採取之行動，<sup>19</sup> 包括透過全球環境基金理事會關於與各公約及國際機構關係之決議所採取之行動；<br />\n(b) [所有] 合格締約方[，包括開發中國家，特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家，以及經濟轉型中之締約方] 採取措施申請並獲得及時、充足且可預測之資金，以使其能夠負擔其履行《公約》及其議定書下義務、並產生全球環境效益之措施所產生的約定全額增量成本之程度；<br />\n(c) 締約方所提供關於其執行全球環境基金信託基金與全球生物多樣性綱要基金下專案績效之資訊，例如影響該等締約方以及女性與青年的限制因素，以及執行機構之績效；<br />\n(d) 合格締約方中，透過財務機制獲得財務支持以執行全球生物多樣性目標與指標（包括與《公約》及其議定書相關之目標與指標）之百分比；<br />\n(e) 透過財務機制，用於支持達成全球生物多樣性目標與指標中，與生物多樣性相關之資金百分比；<br />\n(f) 共同融資之趨勢，特別是透過財務機制在生物多樣性重點領域所促成之私人及非撥款型融資趨勢；<br />\n(g) 在財務機制下，資助全球、區域及次區域生物多樣性專案之趨勢；<br />\n(h) 考量到全球環境基金已被指定以持續及臨時方式運作其財務機制之各公約間綜效，其資助趨勢；<br />\n(i) 考量到生物多樣性相關公約與協議間綜效，針對該等公約與協議之資助趨勢；<br />\n(j) 專案開發與資源撥付時程之趨勢，包括專案核准至首次撥款之間的時間；<br />\n(k) 針對或由原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年之資助趨勢，包括取得資金模式之進展；<br />\n(l) 使締約方與利害關係人能夠確保取得全球環境基金資金之能力建構活動，其數量與主題之趨勢；</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"<sup>19</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。","html":"<p><sup>19</sup> 決議 15/4，附件。</p>","en":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"md":"14/15","html":"<p>14/15</p>","en":[15,16,17,18,19]}]},{"p":"p015","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae4aaca496641e2d89deda4/p015.md","en":[{"t":"CBD/COP/17/L.20"},{"t":"[(m) Trends in project financing leading to high sustainability or durability ratings and long-term results achieved through biodiversity programming supported by the Global Environment Facility in relation to expected results planned by the Facility through that programming;]"},{"t":"[(n)   Criteria listed in decision 16/34 of 27 February 2025.]"},{"t":"5.     The assessment should include a comparison of the Global Environment Facility with the financial mechanisms of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including the Green Climate Fund, the Adaptation Fund and the Fund for Responding to Loss and Damage. Elements for consideration should include: contributor base; funding modalities and financial performance; criteria and processes for funding, including project cycle considerations; access and disbursement modalities (e.g. direct allocation or project-based disbursement), including for indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth; relationship between the governing body of the fund and the Conference of the Parties to the respective multilateral environmental agreement; transparency, monitoring, reporting and evaluation; accreditation process and role and performance of implementing agencies; cost-effectiveness of operations; ability to leverage funding to mobilize additional finance for biodiversity; cost of setting up and running the financial instrument; leveraging public and private co-finance; and integration of various environmental fields."},{"t":"D.    Procedures for implementation"},{"t":"6.    In consultation with the Bureau, the Executive Secretary will contract an experienced independent evaluator to undertake the review, in accordance with the aforementioned objectives, methodology and criteria."},{"t":"7.    The evaluator will undertake desk studies, questionnaire surveys, interviews and field visits, such as may be required for the implementation of the review, and collaborate for that purpose with the Global Environment Facility and its Independent Evaluation Office, as well as other independent assessments, such as those of the Multilateral Performance Network, if necessary, and prepare a compilation and synthesis of the information received."},{"t":"8.     Special efforts should be made to collect the views of Parties, indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth, including, as applicable, information on possible impacts on their rights, and of the private sector and non-governmental organizations, in relation to project-specific environmental objectives and in accordance with relevant national legislation."},{"t":"9.   The draft synthesis report and recommendations of the evaluator will be made available to the Global Environment Facility for its review and comments. Such comments will be included in the documentation and identified by source."},{"t":"10. The report should include as an annex the study requested in paragraph 41 of decision 16/33 of 27 February 2025 [benchmarking the Global Environment Facility against the financial mechanisms or similar instruments of other relevant multilateral environmental agreements, including with regard to their legal nature, funding modalities and financial performance, criteria and process for funding, access and disbursement modalities, monitoring and evaluation, governance and the cost-effectiveness of operations[, as well as other criteria contained in decision 16/34]]."},{"t":"11.   The report shall include as an annex the stocktake review referred to in decision 15/15."},{"t":"12. On the basis of the synthesis report and recommendations of the independent evaluator, the Executive Secretary will prepare, in consultation with the Council and the Secretariat of the Global Environment Facility, a draft decision on the seventh quadrennial review of the financial mechanism, including specific suggestions for action to improve the effectiveness of the mechanism, as necessary, for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Implementation, with its recommendations to be submitted to the Conference of the Parties at its eighteenth meeting."},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"15/15"}],"blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/L.20","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/L.20</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[(m) 專案融資趨勢，其導致高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫預期達成之成果之關係；]\n[(n)\n2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中所列之標準。]","html":"<p>[(m) 專案融資趨勢，其導致高永續性或耐久性評級，以及透過全球環境基金支持之生物多樣性計畫所達成之長期成果，與該基金透過該計畫預期達成之成果之關係；]<br />\n[(n)<br />\n2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/34 中所列之標準。]</p>","en":[1,2]},{"md":"5.\n評估應包含全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金、適應基金及損失與損害基金。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資助模式與財務績效；資助之標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付模式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之模式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監控、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以為生物多樣性動員額外資金之能力；建立與運行該財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n評估應包含全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議財務機制之比較，包括綠色氣候基金、適應基金及損失與損害基金。應考慮之要素應包括：出資者基礎；資助模式與財務績效；資助之標準與程序，包括專案週期之考量；取得與撥付模式（例如：直接分配或以專案為基礎之撥付），包括針對原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之模式；基金管理機構與各自多邊環境協議締約方大會之間之關係；透明度、監控、報告與評估；認證程序以及執行機構之角色與績效；營運之成本效益；利用資金槓桿以為生物多樣性動員額外資金之能力；建立與運行該財務工具之成本；槓桿化公共與私人共同融資；以及各種環境領域之整合。</p>","en":[3,4]},{"md":"D.\n實施程序","html":"<p>D.<br />\n實施程序</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"6.\n執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一名經驗豐富的獨立評估人員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n執行秘書應在諮詢主席團後，聘請一名經驗豐富的獨立評估人員，根據前述目標、方法與標準進行審查。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"7.\n評估人員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視審查實施之需要而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室合作，必要時亦與其他獨立評估機構（如多邊績效網絡）合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n評估人員應進行書面研究、問卷調查、訪談與實地考察（視審查實施之需要而定），並為此目的與全球環境基金及其獨立評估辦公室合作，必要時亦與其他獨立評估機構（如多邊績效網絡）合作，並編製所收資訊之彙編與綜合報告。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"8.\n應特別努力收集締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之意見，包括（視適用情況）關於其權利可能受影響之資訊，以及私營部門與非政府組織之意見，其內容應與特定專案之環境目標相關，並符合相關國家立法。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n應特別努力收集締約方、原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年之意見，包括（視適用情況）關於其權利可能受影響之資訊，以及私營部門與非政府組織之意見，其內容應與特定專案之環境目標相關，並符合相關國家立法。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"9.\n評估人員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。此類評論應納入文件並標明來源。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n評估人員之綜合報告草案與建議將提供予全球環境基金進行審查與評論。此類評論應納入文件並標明來源。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"10. 報告應包含一項附件，即 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/33 第 41 段所要求之研究[將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助模式與財務績效、資助之標準與程序、取得與撥付模式、監控與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中所含之其他標準]]。","html":"<p>10. 報告應包含一項附件，即 2025 年 2 月 27 日決議 16/33 第 41 段所要求之研究[將全球環境基金與其他相關多邊環境協議之財務機制或類似工具進行基準比較，包括其法律性質、資助模式與財務績效、資助之標準與程序、取得與撥付模式、監控與評估、治理以及營運之成本效益[, 以及決議 16/34 中所含之其他標準]]。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"11.\n報告應包含一項附件，即決議 15/15 中所提及之進度審查。","html":"<p>11.<br />\n報告應包含一項附件，即決議 15/15 中所提及之進度審查。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"12. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估人員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金理事會與秘書處後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，必要時應包含旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議，供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。\n__________","html":"<p>12. 執行秘書應根據獨立評估人員之綜合報告與建議，並在諮詢全球環境基金理事會與秘書處後，準備一份關於財務機制第七次四年一度審查之決議草案，必要時應包含旨在提高機制有效性之具體行動建議，供執行附屬機構審議，其建議應提交至第十八次締約方大會。</p>\n<hr />","en":[11]},{"md":"15/15","html":"<p>15/15</p>","pre":"次締約方大會。\n__________\n\n","en":[12,13]}]}]};
